From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <nottzaid@tutamail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:14:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] miles-bench: deferred command recording through a
 replay worker (VKD3D_BENCH_CMD_REPLAY=1)

Command lists' Vulkan command buffers record into per-buffer op streams that one worker thread
replays into the driver, taking the driver's recording cost (~20% of the render thread) off the
critical path. Same calls, same arguments, same order per command buffer. Wrappers for every device
function that can see a command buffer are generated (cmdreplay_gen.py) so a tagged handle never
reaches the driver; pool operations, submission and destroys order themselves after the worker.
